Subject: [PATCH] qcacld: test the disconnect source for MLO link switch

lim_process_sb_disconnect_req() compared the 802.11 reason code with
CM_MLO_LINK_SWITCH_DISCONNECT, a wlan_cm_source value, so a link-switch
disconnect was never kept off the air. Test req->req.source, as the
disconnect handler further down already does and as newer qcacld-3.0
(FP6 modules, lineage-23.2) does. clang 20 rejects the mixed-enum
comparison (-Wenum-compare, -Werror).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
--- a/qcacld-3.0/core/mac/src/pe/lim/lim_process_sme_req_messages.c
+++ b/qcacld-3.0/core/mac/src/pe/lim/lim_process_sme_req_messages.c
@@ -4820,7 +4820,7 @@
 		disassoc_req.doNotSendOverTheAir = 1;
 		disassoc_req.reasonCode =
 					REASON_AUTHORIZED_ACCESS_LIMIT_REACHED;
-	} else if (req->req.reason_code == CM_MLO_LINK_SWITCH_DISCONNECT) {
+	} else if (req->req.source == CM_MLO_LINK_SWITCH_DISCONNECT) {
 		disassoc_req.doNotSendOverTheAir = 1;
 	}

